  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the coin dash game in src/main.ts. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so I haven't seen it render or play.\n\n**Game rules**\n- **Arena and coins:** a sphere player moves on a flat arena with arrow keys or WASD. There are 10 coins, and a new one spawns whenever one is collected. Spawn positions come from a seeded RNG that resets on restart, so rounds are deterministic.\n- **Round limits:** the status becomes `won` as soon as the score reaches 15. It becomes `lost` when the timer reaches 30 s.\n- **Pause and restart:** `P` pauses and `R` restarts. `R` also clears a pause.\n\n**Simulation**\n- It runs at a fixed 1/60 s step with an accumulator. Time is `frame / 60`.\n- `window.__EVAL__.step(n)` runs `n` fixed steps immediately with the current input state. While paused, or after the round ends, it does nothing.\n\n**HUD and rendering**\n- The DOM HUD sits below the canvas, with elements `#score`, `#time` (remaining seconds) and `#status`.\n- Rendering uses Aura3D's `createAuraApp(\"#app\")` with primitives, the \"outdoor-day\" look and a perspective camera. `resize: false` keeps the canvas size.\n- A separate `requestAnimationFrame` loop drives the simulation and moves the scene nodes. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\n**Failure handling**\n- If the Aura3D mount fails, the game logic and `__EVAL__` still work, but nothing is drawn.\n\n",
